usage() {
    cat <<'EOF'
Run the guided Workerd-on-Hyperlight feature demos.

Usage:
  tools/hyperlight-demo [--output-dir DIR] [--verbose] [--all]
  tools/hyperlight-demo [--output-dir DIR] [--verbose] --demo NAME
  tools/hyperlight-demo --list
  tools/hyperlight-demo --preview
  tools/hyperlight-demo --describe NAME
  tools/hyperlight-demo --clear
  tools/hyperlight-demo --help

With no selection, the runner presents each demo interactively. Logs and
ordinary demo output are written below demo-output/ by default.

Options:
  --all             Run every demo without presenter pauses
  --demo NAME       Run one named demo
  --list            Show the formatted feature menu
  --preview         Render the complete presenter narration without running
  --describe NAME   Render one demo's narration without running
  --clear           Remove this checkout's generated demo output and exit
  --output-dir DIR  Override the output directory
  --benchmark-requests N
                    Total requests for benchmark-on-demand/benchmark-prewarmed
                    only (default: 100 x physical cores)
  --benchmark-concurrency N
                    Concurrent hey requests for every benchmark-* demo
                    (default: physical cores). For benchmark-resident,
                    benchmark-multi-app, and benchmark-orchestrator-contract
                    this is an aggregate across all --benchmark-apps apps and
                    must not exceed --benchmark-load-requests
  --benchmark-vms N Concurrent request-execution VMs, benchmark-on-demand/
                    benchmark-prewarmed only; ignored by benchmark-resident/
                    benchmark-multi-app/benchmark-orchestrator-contract
                    (default: physical cores)
  --benchmark-pool-vms N
                    Prewarmed ready inventory, benchmark-prewarmed only;
                    ignored by every other benchmark-* demo (default:
                    physical cores + 1; must be at least 2)
  --benchmark-apps N
                    Independent/routed apps for benchmark-resident,
                    benchmark-multi-app, and benchmark-orchestrator-contract
                    (default: physical cores)
  --benchmark-load-requests N
                    Aggregate requests for those same three benchmarks,
                    distributed evenly across --benchmark-apps apps
                    (default: --benchmark-apps x 1000)
  --benchmark-hey-parallel N
                    Max concurrent hey client processes for benchmark-resident/
                    benchmark-multi-app/benchmark-orchestrator-contract
                    (default: --benchmark-apps -- every app's hey process
                    launches in a single synchronized wave, not split into
                    sequential wave_1-finishes-then-wave_2-starts batches).
                    Lower it to cap concurrent OS processes competing for
                    CPU/loopback sockets and restore (bounded) wave-splitting
  --benchmark-hey-ramp-ms N
                    Every hey process is forked paused and released together
                    as a batch; this adds a per-job delay (milliseconds)
                    before each one actually starts sending requests, timed
                    from its position in the batch (default: 10, so the
                    default single-wave launch above ramps up rather than
                    hitting the CPU in the same instant; set to 0 for every
                    job to release at once). Applies to every hey launch
                    site (the three load benchmarks above, benchmark-on-
                    demand/benchmark-prewarmed, and the orchestrator-contract
                    drain test); costs roughly (batch_size - 1) x N ms of
                    extra wall-clock per wave
  --verbose         Stream raw command output as well as saving it
  -h, --help        Show this help
EOF
}

